about:
Jesse is a Partner with PwC based out of the Toronto office. As part of the Technology Strategy & Transformation team he advises clients how to develop technology-driven business strategies. He takes particular interest in applying innovative technologies and digital engagement approaches to solve complex business issues, optimizing operating models for efficient service delivery, and planning for large-scale industry disruption.

The clients he advises operate in many diverse industries, both in the private and public sector, nationally and internationally. 

A few examples of his recent engagement experience include:
• supported the launch of an entirely new provincial institution, including development of core departmental structures, tendering of strategic operational contracts, and onboarding of initial staff;
• designed a shared services strategy to consolidate IT operations across multiple disparate agencies within Canada’s largest municipality;
• established a future state operating model and transition plan for Canada’s largest IT shared service organization;
• developed a long-term strategic roadmap for technology enablement and adoption at a major Canadian airport;
• provided directional guidance and financial analysis for an acquisition by an international private equity firm; 
• developed a digital strategy to enhance multi-directional digital connections amongst citizens, business, employees and government for a large Canadian municipality; and
• designed a retail strategy integrating digital and brick-and-mortar elements for a prominent sports and entertainment organization.

Finally, Jesse was recently presented with the 2013 PwC National CEO award and a 2016 Spotlight award for outstanding client services, a testament to his hard work and dedication to quality.

experience.description:
•	Implementation of measures, processes and systems within manufacturing at the business system level to identify opportunities to enhance performance (productivity and efficiency) and improve by using Six Sigma tools and processes; 
•	Support to KPIs in the manufacturing plants within the business system and coordinating improvement activities, but also leading and participating in individual projects and/or relevant initiatives; 
•	Development and implementation of the Continuous Improvement Program (CIP) in cooperation with production strategy management at the business group level by creating a culture of continuous improvement through maximising process capability, flexibility and capacity; 
•	Support to managers and employees at all CI levels, as well as relevant training activities and development of employees through the optimization of business processes; 
•	Improvements measurement and cost savings, evaluation of processes and procedures with the Senior Team against best practices in the field; driving business improvement and integration of processes and people towards achievement of corporate strategies; 
•	Initiating and maintaining cooperation with plant managers in terms of CI and implementation of new business methods in general with the focus on using data to identify trends in poor performance and root cause identification supported by relevant analytical techniques; 
•	Assisting in resolution of key process issues, guidance for process change where necessary and continual development and maintenance of the improvement culture within the organization.
•	Assisting with selection of projects and  project mentoring where required and also full mentoring for a number of Six Sigma and other improvement initiatives, 
•	Delivering training for Lean and Six Sigma tools and techniques, as well as coaching Green Belt resources to deliver the training in their own areas.

